  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{侮|あなど}る.\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in the negative form {侮|あなど}れない (not to be underestimated), which functions as a compliment meaning \"formidable\" or \"not to be taken lightly.\" The positive form {侮|あなど}る carries a warning or critical tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {相手|あいて}を{侮|あなど}る: to underestimate an opponent\n- {敵|てき}を{侮|あなど}る: to underestimate the enemy\n- {侮|あなど}れない{存在|そんざい}: a force not to be underestimated\n- {侮|あなど}りがたい: formidable, not to be scorned\n\nCOMMON PATTERN:\n〜を{侮|あなど}ってはいけない / 〜を{侮|あなど}るな: \"Don't underestimate ~\" — a frequent warning pattern.\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {侮|あなど}る also appears in {侮辱|ぶじょく} (insult, contempt), which is the on'yomi compound.",
